<figure class="system-map system-map-theophonia" aria-labelledby="theophonia-map-title">
  <figcaption id="theophonia-map-title">
    <span class="map-kicker">Pipeline architecture</span>
    <strong>Every stage must preserve the source</strong>
    <span>Language models handle language. Deterministic state, evidence, and gates control the workflow.</span>
  </figcaption>

  <div class="map-track map-track-five" role="list">
    <div class="map-node" role="listitem">
      <span class="map-index">01</span>
      <strong>Map the recording</strong>
      <p>Voice activity detection locates speech and exposes missing coverage.</p>
      <small>Audio clock · speech windows</small>
    </div>
    <div class="map-node" role="listitem">
      <span class="map-index">02</span>
      <strong>Transcribe Greek</strong>
      <p>Whisper large v3 works in windows. Failed gaps return to transcription.</p>
      <small>GPU speech recognition · coverage check</small>
    </div>
    <div class="map-node" role="listitem">
      <span class="map-index">03</span>
      <strong>Ground and translate</strong>
      <p>Indexed scripture, liturgy, and patristic sources support specialist terms.</p>
      <small>SQLite retrieval · stable passages</small>
    </div>
    <div class="map-node" role="listitem">
      <span class="map-index">04</span>
      <strong>Audit meaning</strong>
      <p>Greek and English passages are reviewed together. Findings cite exact evidence.</p>
      <small>Structured review · risk evidence</small>
    </div>
    <div class="map-node map-node-accent" role="listitem">
      <span class="map-index">05</span>
      <strong>Repair or hold</strong>
      <p>Only affected passages rerun. Unresolved work cannot pass the release gate.</p>
      <small>Targeted repair · fail closed output</small>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="map-spine">
    <span>SQLite task ledger</span>
    <span>SHA 256 artifact lineage</span>
    <span>Leases and retries</span>
    <span>Separate execution and quality states</span>
  </div>
</figure>
